# 🐧 Linux Simulator

## 🚀 Development

Linux Simulator was created as a learning project to practice Python programming and develop skills in building larger, more organized systems.

The initial idea was to build an interactive, terminal-based environment. Over time, the project evolved and gained new features, such as:

* 📁 Folder management
* 💻 Interactive terminal
* 🌐 Simulated web browser
* 🧮 Calculator
* 🎮 Games
* 📅 Calendar
* 🕐 Brasília Time clock

Throughout development, various tests, bug fixes, and code organization improvements were carried out.

## 🛠️ Technologies and Concepts Used

### 🐍 Python 3

The primary language used to develop the entire project.

### 🧱 Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

Used to better organize the code through classes, methods, and objects.

### 🔧 Functions

Employed to break the program down into smaller parts, facilitating code maintenance and reusability.

### 🔀 Conditional Structures

Used to control menus, user choices, and feature operations.

### 🔁 Loop Structures

Responsible for keeping menus active and executing repetitive tasks.

### 📋 Lists and Dictionaries

Used to store and organize system and game information.

### ⚠️ Exception Handling

Applied to prevent errors caused by invalid user input.

### 📅 Date and Time

Used to implement features such as the calendar and clock.

### 💻 Terminal Interface (CLI)

All user interaction takes place via the terminal, simulating an operating system environment. ## 🎯 Key Takeaways

